   "html": "<p>Peacock tapped IHC to break through an oversaturated market during an unprecedented period of industry strikes. The result was a fan-first stunt that captured the attention and hearts of Comic-Con attendees.</p>\n<p>Led by Sweet Tooth himself, we organized an in-world, post-apocalyptical marching band through the Gaslamp Quarters in San Diego. The musicians played all Y2K and 90s hits while the immersive talent shared key tune-in messaging and rallied the crowd to come see the clown villain’s “show” later that day. </p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "street stunt & marching band",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text2",
     "left": "<p>Sweet Tooth led the marching band through the Gaslamp District towards the Twisted Metal lot, for a surprise performance from his favorite artist, the Silver Haired God himself: Sisqo! Along the way, the procession grew as fans joined in from the streets towards the main stage.</p>",
     "right": "<p>We had 6 members from the <a href=\"https://www.lamarchingband.com/\"><strong>LA Marching Band</strong></a> play pump-up, Y2K-leaning songs along the marching path. The band was dressed as ‘in-world’ characters and with dirtied up instruments including a trumpet, saxophone, trombone, sousaphone, snare drum and bass drum.</p>"
    },
